      "content": "I'm a bit confused by the comparison to \"goblin clans\" and \"goblin lords.\" I'm trying to build a formal site report for a peer-reviewed journal, so I really need to keep the analysis strictly within the bounds of archaeological theory and taphonomy. \n\nCan we skip the analogies and focus on the taphonomic side? Specifically, if we're looking at Sector B, what specific indicators in the stratigraphic profile or the soil matrix would suggest that the \"erratic\" nature of the assemblage is due to post-depositional disturbance (like bioturbation or heavy agricultural ploughing) rather than an actual variation in the ancient production methods?",
      "source": "evaluator"
